1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,270
Ming.

2
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,110
Ming.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,190
Mom,

4
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,550
what's wrong?

5
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,920
I was just worried about
leaving you home alone,

6
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,280
so I wanted to come back
and check on you.

7
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:35,640
Mom.

8
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,560
I had a sudden surge of panic just now.

9
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,330
I kept feeling like something
bad was happening to you,

10
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:42,100
so I had to check on you.

11
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:44,220
I'm glad you're okay.

12
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,770
If anything happened to you,

13
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,790
I wouldn't know how to face
your father when I pass on.

14
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:51,640
Mom,

15
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,920
how could anything happen to me?

16
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,110
Son,

17
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,710
what is going on?

18
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,630
Why did a vision of you
having an accident

19
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:05,300
suddenly flash through my mind just now?

20
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:08,000
My memories have been
so confused lately.

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:08,640
Mom,

22
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:11,070
what did you remember?

23
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:12,680
Take your time and tell me.

24
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,350
I'll explain everything
to you step by step.

25
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:20,310
Son,

26
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:23,280
look at the treat I bought for you.

27
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:36,950
Ming...

28
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:39,310
Ming, what's wrong with you?

29
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,070
Ming...

30
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:44,310
I am back.

31
00:01:46,070 --> 00:01:48,560
What's wrong with you, Ming?

32
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:52,070
Don't be afraid, I am back.

33
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,790
I am here.

34
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,150
I shouldn't have left you home alone.

35
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:00,040
Ming, I am taking you to the hospital.

36
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,000
Don't be afraid.

37
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,760
It's okay...

38
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,400
Son...

39
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:11,400
Ming!

40
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,190
- Mom!
- Ming!

41
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:12,840
Mom!

42
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:13,840
Mom, what's wrong?

43
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,560
Mom!

44
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:16,000
What's wrong with you?

45
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:26,960
Why is it in my memory

46
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:30,080
that you were murdered
when you were five?

47
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,710
I shouldn't have
left you home alone that day.

48
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:35,680
Mom, what else do you
remember about that day?

49
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,680
Tell me.

50
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,470
When your father was on a mission,

51
00:02:42,190 --> 00:02:43,590
he was shot by
the killer's handmade gun.

52
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,630
I took you to identify his body.

53
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,680
What time was it when you
took me to identify the body?

54
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:53,080
Before I got off work that day,

55
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:55,400
I received a call
from your father's unit.

56
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,190
And what time was it
when I was murdered?

57
00:02:57,590 --> 00:02:59,240
Son, are you doing

58
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,840
something dangerous?

59
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:02,870
Whatever it is, please stop doing it.

60
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:05,120
Can't we just keep
living our lives as they are?

61
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,840
I've already lost your father.

62
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,470
And I can't lose you.

63
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:10,190
Mom, think carefully again.

64
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,470
What else do you actually remember?

65
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,960
I don't remember.

66
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,360
It feels like I suddenly
jumped to the present,

67
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,960
and I don't remember
anything in between.

68
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:29,460
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 12=

69
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:36,710
(Back in 1990,)

70
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:39,240
(if Qin was killed,)

71
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,680
(then Mom would take me)

72
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,150
(to identify Qin's body.)

73
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,630
(Mom and I would have
escaped the killer.)

74
00:03:45,910 --> 00:03:47,310
(But if Qin wasn't killed,)

75
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,590
(the killer)

76
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,470
(would have killed
my younger self and Mom.)

77
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,710
(In this altered history,)

78
00:03:56,910 --> 00:03:58,710
(not only was Qin's fate changed,)

79
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:02,680
(but the killer's
trajectory was also changed.)

80
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,270
Alright.

81
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:27,120
Let's see

82
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,560
who can outrun time, then.

83
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,270
Qin.

84
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:46,390
Can you hear me, Qin?

85
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,040
Captain,

86
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,390
the comms signal is terrible.

87
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,190
I'll go check if Zhang Xiaoshan
has been brought over.

88
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:53,070
Alright, go ahead.

89
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,240
What a dump.

90
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,750
I saved Qin

91
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:14,830
but doomed Mom and myself instead.

92
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,600
I'm not saving anyone at all.

93
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,750
I'm just robbing Peter to pay Paul.

94
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,120
There must be something else.

95
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:24,560
I must have missed something.

96
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,040
The killer's target was me.

97
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:28,870
It was me.

98
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:34,160
Qin.

99
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:37,070
Currently, during this
period of high sunspot activity,

100
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:39,510
we've observed
dense clusters of sunspots,

101
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,190
an increase in solar
prominences at the edge,

102
00:05:41,430 --> 00:05:43,310
(Period of high sunspot activity)
and more coronal mass ejections.

103
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:45,800
(Solar activity impacts communications)
They hit the magnetic field and ionosphere,

104
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:48,560
causing fluctuations in signal channels.

105
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,270
Some communication
frequency bands will shut down.

106
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:54,160
Even right under the tower
with the strongest signal,

107
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:55,480
you won't be able to communicate.

108
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,480
Ming.

109
00:05:58,870 --> 00:05:59,950
Ming, can you hear me, Ming?

110
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,000
Ming.

111
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,480
Ming.

112
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:05,310
Ming.

113
00:06:05,510 --> 00:06:07,120
Ming.

114
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:15,430
Ming.

115
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,720
Ming, can you hear me, Ming?

116
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:18,310
Please answer if you hear me, Ming.

117
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:22,040
Mr. Know-It-All,
are you looking for Dad?

118
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,680
Dad isn't home.

119
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,870
He told me to watch the walkie-talkie.

120
00:06:25,870 --> 00:06:27,310
I can pass a message to him.

121
00:06:27,390 --> 00:06:28,430
No, I'm looking for you.

122
00:06:28,870 --> 00:06:29,950
Listen to me.

123
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,270
Call Mr. Zhou.

124
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,430
Tell Mr. Zhou

125
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,270
there is a real gun inside
the box at the paper mill.

126
00:06:34,270 --> 00:06:35,040
Your dad will die.

127
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:35,830
Say it three times.

128
00:06:35,830 --> 00:06:36,620
After saying all this,

129
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:37,410
go to the hospital to find Mom.

130
00:06:37,410 --> 00:06:39,000
Have Mom take you to
the Public Security Bureau to find Dad.

131
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:39,720
Did you hear me?

132
00:06:40,190 --> 00:06:41,430
Paper box, what?

133
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:42,920
What happened to Mr. Zhou?

134
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:44,480
He can't remember all that.

135
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:46,310
I'll repeat it.

136
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,040
Paper mill. In the box. Real gun.

137
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,390
Call Mr. Zhou and tell him.

138
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:51,270
Your dad will die.

139
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:52,600
Then go to the hospital to find Mom.

140
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,480
Did you hear me?

141
00:06:54,190 --> 00:06:56,510
I can't remember, Mr. Know-It-All.

142
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,800
He still can't remember.

143
00:06:58,870 --> 00:06:59,680
Then...

144
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:01,930
Find a piece of paper and write it down.

145
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,190
Find a piece of paper and write it down.

146
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,390
If you don't do as I say,

147
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,560
Dad will find out right away

148
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,750
that you broke the star on his medal.

149
00:07:07,750 --> 00:07:09,830
Don't, don't tell him.

150
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,560
I don't know how to write.

151
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:16,160
You don't know how to write?

152
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,310
You know how to draw, right?

153
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,600
Draw a box.

154
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,950
A cardboard box. A square.

155
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:29,040
Done drawing.

156
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:31,720
Now, draw a real gun. Draw a handgun.

157
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:43,070
Done drawing.

158
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:48,270
Mr. Know-It-All.

159
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:49,000
Ming.

160
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,310
Mr. Know-It-All.

161
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,360
Ming.

162
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,040
Ming.

163
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:04,630
Hello?

164
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:05,680
Mr. Zhou.

165
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,390
What?

166
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:08,390
I'm looking for Mr. Zhou,
the medical examiner.

167
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:09,160
Section Chief Zhou.

168
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:11,480
What's up?

169
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,630
There's a phone call for you.

170
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:13,950
Who is it?

171
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,920
It's a kid. Sounds pretty anxious.

172
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:18,190
Hello?

173
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:19,830
Mr. Zhou, save us.

174
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,390
Dad's gun is in...

175
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,390
What gun?

176
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,310
Are you looking for your dad?

177
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:26,240
No, I'm not looking for Dad.

178
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,830
Mr. Zhou, go save Dad.

179
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,120
In the box,

180
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,080
there is a gun.

181
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:35,600
Mr. Zhou, hurry and save Dad.

182
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:38,840
What's wrong, Section Chief Zhou?

183
00:08:39,550 --> 00:08:40,750
It was Qin's son.

184
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,960
He's being all mysterious,

185
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,960
saying something about a gun in a box

186
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,270
and telling me to go save his dad.

187
00:08:45,550 --> 00:08:46,720
Is he fooling around?

188
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:47,960
Watched too many cop movies?

189
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,120
I don't know.

190
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:52,240
I've already told Mr. Zhou.

191
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:54,030
Don't tell Dad

192
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:56,150
that I was the one who broke his medal.

193
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:58,200
I'm going to go find Mom now.

194
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,270
Ming.

195
00:09:14,030 --> 00:09:14,840
Ming.

196
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:16,720
Mom.

197
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,120
What's wrong?

198
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,790
All right.

199
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:21,870
We can't be late.

200
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:26,150
No, we have to go now. We must go.

201
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,630
Mom, take me to Dad.

202
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:29,080
Okay.

203
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,270
I want to find Dad now.

204
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:31,870
Hurry up.

205
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:33,390
- Ming, don't cry.
- It's very dangerous.

206
00:09:33,390 --> 00:09:34,960
Okay, I will take you there.

207
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,670
We'll go find Dad now, okay?

208
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,550
- All right, stop crying.
- Hurry.

209
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,200
Hey,

210
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:42,030
is Qin out on a mission?

211
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,120
Yes.

212
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:44,480
What's up?

213
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:49,150
Is there anything
related to boxes or crates?

214
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:50,750
Boxes? Crates?

215
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:51,440
Yes.

216
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,510
A message just came in.

217
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,080
It said they were pursuing a suspect

218
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,550
and tracked him to the Daxin Paper Mill.

219
00:09:57,750 --> 00:10:00,320
Paper mill... Boxes...

220
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:03,240
How did this kid know?

221
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:07,910
Quick.

222
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:08,440
What's happened?

223
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,270
The suspect has a gun.

224
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:10,670
- A gun?
- Notify Qin now.

225
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:11,670
Hurry.

226
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,750
Captain Qin,

227
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:14,150
please respond if you hear me.
Captain Qin.

228
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:17,000
Hello, Qin.

229
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:17,910
Can you hear me?

230
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:19,270
The suspect has a gun.

231
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:20,480
Qin!

232
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,030
My dear Ming,

233
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:36,240
I called you so many times.

234
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,480
Why didn't you answer?

235
00:10:37,510 --> 00:10:40,080
We found the eyewitnesses
for Ding Hua and Li Tingxiang.

236
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,390
What's wrong? What's going on lately?

237
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,080
What did the witness say?

238
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,910
A neighbor of the Li Tingxiang couple,

239
00:10:53,910 --> 00:10:55,120
an elderly man,

240
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,030
said that around 5:30 PM,

241
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:59,450
- he saw a panicked stranger.
- What's the rush?

242
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,340
- He wasn't a resident of that building.
- Such ill-mannered trash.

243
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:04,000
Could he be a tenant?

244
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,240
It's an old neighborhood.

245
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:07,390
The old man said
he's lived there for over 20 years.

246
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,550
He knows with his eyes closed

247
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:09,980
who lives in which building and unit.

248
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:10,750
Surveillance footage was found.

249
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:11,550
Let's go check it out.

250
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:15,440
Rewind it a bit.

251
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,870
Let's see where he went.

252
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,000
He went toward Huaxin Street.

253
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,750
I'll have someone pull
the street surveillance.

254
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:25,600
Was he alone?

255
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,030
The old man said
the suspicious person he saw

256
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:27,870
was the only one.

257
00:11:28,910 --> 00:11:29,720
Could it be

258
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,670
that one person really dual-wielded?

259
00:11:33,910 --> 00:11:35,120
Do you still suspect

260
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:36,960
there were two killers at the scene?

261
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:38,600
But the surveillance, the witness,

262
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,790
and the cross-match results all show

263
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:41,200
there was only one killer at the scene.

264
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,630
Li Tingxiang's body tells me

265
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:44,150
there were two killers at the scene.

266
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,290
While fighting the first killer,

267
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:56,740
the victim was stabbed in
the chest and finally collapsed,

268
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:58,060
(Killer 1, Killer 2)
losing the ability to resist.

269
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:58,910
After that,

270
00:11:58,930 --> 00:12:00,270
(Precise strike to the back)
the second killer appeared

271
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,600
and stabbed them from
behind to finish them off.

272
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:05,060
(At least two people present)

273
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:05,920
(Victim stabbed
from the front, collapsed)

274
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,860
(Killer forced victim
from guest room to balcony)

275
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:07,260
(Killer)

276
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:11,440
Impossible.

277
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,480
The scene examination
results don't support that.

278
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:16,790
There are dozens of
bloody footprints at the scene.

279
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:18,200
None of which belong to the two victims.

280
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,240
This shows that after losing
the ability to resist, they fell quickly

281
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,480
and never got back up.

282
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:22,390
The complete bloody footprints

283
00:12:22,390 --> 00:12:23,670
and the partial ones

284
00:12:23,670 --> 00:12:24,840
all came from a man

285
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,320
who is about 175 cm tall.

286
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,200
It can be confirmed

287
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,200
that these footprints
belong to the killer.

288
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:30,910
What about
the remaining partial footprints?

289
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:33,150
After comparison,
the other partial footprints

290
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:34,390
were all found to originate

291
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:36,630
from several neighbors who
initially entered the crime scene

292
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,360
and

293
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:39,080
the victim's son, Li Yan.

294
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:39,910
In other words,

295
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,600
apart from those
who entered after the crime,

296
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,150
there is currently only one unassigned

297
00:12:44,150 --> 00:12:44,870
suspect footprint.

298
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:45,870
From this, we deduce

299
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:47,120
that there was only
one killer at the scene.

300
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:49,240
Right. At a scene covered in blood,

301
00:12:49,390 --> 00:12:51,720
anyone entering
would leave bloody footprints.

302
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:53,840
Unless he was floating.

303
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,600
That's not right.

304
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,550
Li Tingxiang's body tells me otherwise.

305
00:12:58,550 --> 00:12:59,720
If you were the killer,

306
00:12:59,910 --> 00:13:01,360
would you bring two daggers,

307
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,670
one to stab the chest,

308
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:04,320
and another to
finish him off in the back?

309
00:13:08,270 --> 00:13:09,080
Hello?

310
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:11,000
Okay.

311
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,390
The suspect from
the surveillance video has been found.

312
00:13:13,390 --> 00:13:13,790
Chief Song,

313
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:14,960
I'll go bring him in first.

314
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:15,840
Alright.

315
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,390
Hello, room service.

316
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:27,720
Quick, after him!

317
00:13:32,910 --> 00:13:33,670
Split up and chase him.

318
00:13:33,670 --> 00:13:34,320
Yes, sir.

319
00:13:45,790 --> 00:13:46,600
Stop right there.

320
00:13:49,690 --> 00:13:50,600
Cut him off from the other side.

321
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,240
Yes, sir!

322
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,750
Split up and search.

323
00:14:16,750 --> 00:14:17,390
Yes, sir.

324
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,240
Let's go.

325
00:15:06,790 --> 00:15:07,600
Don't move.

326
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:16,480
Take him away.

327
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,120
Yes, sir.

328
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,120
Captain Lin,

329
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:25,030
this physical evidence was
found at Zhang Xiaoshan's home.

330
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,300
(Footprint Rubbing)

331
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:36,420
(Bloody Footprint Analysis
and Examination Report)

332
00:16:03,910 --> 00:16:04,750
Zhang Xiaoshan.

333
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,080
Intentional harm,

334
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,910
theft, and robbery.

335
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,320
You sure have quite a rap sheet.

336
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:11,870
You were just released a year ago.

337
00:16:12,270 --> 00:16:13,080
What's the matter?

338
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,390
Are you planning to
make this place your home?

339
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:22,200
Zhang Xiaoshan,

340
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:23,510
where were you

341
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,080
yesterday evening?

342
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,150
Is there something wrong?

343
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,910
Surveillance and witnesses prove

344
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,150
that you appeared at a murder scene.

345
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,870
We found a pair of shoes at your home

346
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:37,790
that perfectly matches
the footprints at the murder scene.

347
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,510
Care to explain?

348
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:41,440
I just went to pick a lock

349
00:16:42,670 --> 00:16:43,790
to get a little cash.

350
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:48,790
When I went in,

351
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,240
there were two dead bodies
lying on the floor.

352
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,600
Scared the heck out of me.

353
00:16:53,750 --> 00:16:55,080
What bad luck.

354
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,600
So I got out of there fast.

355
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,240
That's all there was to it.

356
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:14,550
How is it?

357
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:16,920
He's a tough nut to crack.

358
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,640
No murder weapon was found at his place,

359
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:20,640
just that pair of shoes.

360
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:22,160
I checked his records.

361
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,550
He is a repeat offender.

362
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:25,070
He was in juvenile
detention as a teenager,

363
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:26,920
and his rap sheet got
even worse as he grew up.

364
00:17:27,070 --> 00:17:28,200
With no parental guidance,

365
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,720
let alone any family warmth.

366
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,110
He has no parents.

367
00:17:31,270 --> 00:17:32,400
When he was seven,

368
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,960
his mother committed
suicide by jumping off a building.

369
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:34,720
His father

370
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:35,720
shot a police officer

371
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,720
and was executed by firing squad.

372
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,200
Shot a police officer?

373
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:39,310
Fierce, isn't it?

374
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,110
Doesn't that just prove the saying,

375
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:42,590
"Like father, like son?"

376
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,790
What was his father's name?

377
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,400
Zhang Daxin.

378
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
(Captain Qin Tian died heroically on Oct 16
while pursuing suspect Zhang Daxin)

379
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:17,760
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

380
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:25,610
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

381
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:33,700
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

382
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:39,560
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

383
00:18:41,590 --> 00:18:49,550
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

384
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:55,230
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

385
00:18:57,270 --> 00:19:05,580
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

386
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:11,430
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

387
00:19:12,890 --> 00:19:21,010
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

388
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:26,740
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

389
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:36,560
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

390
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:44,110
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

391
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:48,720
♪Can you hear me?♪

392
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:52,520
♪Can you hear me?♪

393
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:59,980
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

394
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:07,720
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

395
00:20:08,050 --> 00:20:13,660
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

396
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:19,140
♪After all these years♪

397
00:20:21,650 --> 00:20:29,130
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

398
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:31,330
♪And tell you♪

399
00:20:32,550 --> 00:20:35,820
♪I haven't let you down♪
